.TH DEVFIX 1 "August 2026" "DevFix 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
devfix \- network and compatibility helper for Homebrew on Intel macOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B devfix
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
DevFix applies an existing HTTP or SOCKS5 proxy to developer commands without changing the global macOS network configuration. It also diagnoses direct and proxied access to GitHub, the Homebrew API, and Homebrew bottle storage.
.PP
DevFix is not a VPN and does not provide an upstream proxy server.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B doctor [--offline]
Show system, Homebrew, developer-tool, proxy and endpoint diagnostics.
.TP
.B proxy set URL
Save and enable a proxy URL using http, https, socks5, or socks5h.
.TP
.B proxy detect
Try to locate an already-running proxy on common localhost ports.
.TP
.B proxy status
Show configuration with proxy credentials redacted.
.TP
.B on | off
Enable or disable proxy use for commands launched by DevFix.
.TP
.B run COMMAND [ARGS...]
Run an arbitrary command with DevFix-managed environment variables.
.TP
.B brew [ARGS...]
Run Homebrew with DevFix-managed environment variables.
.TP
.B git [ARGS...]
Run git with DevFix-managed environment variables.
.TP
.B curl [ARGS...]
Run curl with DevFix-managed environment variables.
.TP
.B env [--unset]
Print shell commands suitable for eval to apply or clear DevFix variables in the current shell.
.TP
.B mirror set-api URL
Set HOMEBREW_API_DOMAIN.
.TP
.B mirror set-artifact URL
Set HOMEBREW_ARTIFACT_DOMAIN. Only use a trusted mirror.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/devfix/config
Default per-user configuration file. Created with restrictive permissions.
.SH SECURITY
Proxy credentials embedded in a URL are stored in the configuration file. DevFix redacts them from status output. Prefer a local unauthenticated proxy when possible.
.SH SEE ALSO
brew(1), git(1), curl(1)
